{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexProtocol"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper"],"kind":"relationships"},{"title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef"],"type":"conformingTypes","kind":"relationships"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexProtocol\/mutex","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexProtocol\/mutexImpl"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexProtocol\/free()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexProtocol\/getMutexImpl()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexProtocol\/init_()"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex"},{"type":"text","text":" works like a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StaticMutexProtocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib14PointerWrapperP","text":"PointerWrapper","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Prior to GLib 2.32, GStaticMutex had the significant advantage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"that it doesn’t need to be created at run-time, but can be defined","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at compile-time. Since 2.32, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" can be statically allocated"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as well, and GStaticMutex has been deprecated.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is a version of our "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"give_me_next_number()"},{"type":"text","text":" example using"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"a GStaticMutex:"}]},{"code":["  int","  give_me_next_number (void)","  {","    static int current_number = 0;","    int ret_val;","    static GStaticMutex mutex = G_STATIC_MUTEX_INIT;","","    g_static_mutex_lock (&mutex);","    ret_val = current_number = calc_next_number (current_number);","    g_static_mutex_unlock (&mutex);","","    return ret_val;","  }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sometimes you would like to dynamically create a mutex. If you don’t"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"want to require prior calling to "},{"code":"g_thread_init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because your code","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should also be usable in non-threaded programs, you are not able to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"use ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_mutex_new()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and thus "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex","isActive":true},{"text":", as that requires a prior call to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_thread_init()"},{"type":"text","text":". In these cases you can also use a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It must be initialized with "},{"code":"g_static_mutex_init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" before using it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and freed with with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_static_mutex_free()"},{"type":"text","text":" when not needed anymore to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"free up any allocated resources.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Even though ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex"},{"text":" is not opaque, it should only be used with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the following functions, as it is defined differently on different"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"platforms."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All of the g_static_mutex_* functions apart from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_static_mutex_get_mutex()"},{"type":"text","text":" can also be used even if "},{"code":"g_thread_init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"has not yet been called. Then they do nothing, apart from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_static_mutex_trylock()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" which does nothing but returning "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All of the g_static_mutex_* functions are actually macros. Apart from"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"taking their addresses, you can however use them as if they were"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"functions.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexProtocol","isActive":true},{"text":" protocol exposes the methods and properties of an underlying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GStaticMutex"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"The default implementation of these can be found in the protocol extension below."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"For a concrete class that implements these methods and properties, see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Alternatively, use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexRef","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" as a lighweight, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unowned"},{"text":" reference if you already have an instance you just want to use.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StaticMutexProtocol"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:4GLib19StaticMutexProtocolP","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StaticMutexProtocol"}],"title":"StaticMutexProtocol"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/staticmutexprotocol"]}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/PointerWrapper":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PointerWrapper"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Protocol for GLib types that wrap pointers.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/pointerwrapper","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PointerWrapper","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PointerWrapper","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/Mutex":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex"},{"type":"text","text":" struct is an opaque data structure to represent a mutex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(mutual exclusion). It can be used to protect data against shared","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access."}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Mutex","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Mutex","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"Mutex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/mutex"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticMutexProtocol/getMutexImpl()":{"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticmutexprotocol\/getmuteximpl()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"getMutexImpl","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutexRef","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib8MutexRefV"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"getMutexImpl()","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexProtocol\/getMutexImpl()"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticMutexProtocol/free()":{"deprecated":true,"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"free","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticmutexprotocol\/free()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Releases all resources allocated to "},{"code":"mutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutexProtocol\/free()","title":"free()"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticMutexProtocol/init_()":{"deprecated":true,"identifi